# An `else if` ladder thousands deep, each branch nested in the last, and
# a chain of twice as many non-tail calls: a recursion on nesting or on
# call depth in the tools, ours or MLIR's, overflows the small stack they
# keep. Both compile at their size and at twice it, to the ladder's full
# depth of ten thousand, and no count of the work grows faster.
step_limit=120
. "$IDRIS_MLIR_ROOT/harness/testutils.sh"
scale_relation nesting
